<title>USA: U.S., Florida orange crop estimates--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S., Florida orange crop estimates--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA orange production</p>
<p>estimates (crop in 1,000 boxes, yield in gallons/box at 42.0</p>
<p>degrees Brix basis):</p>
<p>    -			1996/97:	Indicated</p>
<p>    -		   Jan 1  Prev.Est.  1995/96</p>
<p> Florida Oranges  220,000   220,000   203,200</p>
<p> Florida Temples    2,500     2,500     2,150</p>
<p> Fla. FCOJ Yield     1.53	1.53	1.52</p>
<p> U.S. Oranges     287,850   285,950   271,790</p>
<p>Note-U.S. oranges and Florida oranges exclude temples.</p>
<p>Florida's record 220.0 million-box crop would be eight percent larger than last season's, USDA said. It would include a record 130.0 million boxes of early and mid-season oranges and 90 million boxes of Valencias, also a record.</p>
<p>U.S. output was forecast for a record large 12.5 million tons, up one percent from last month's estimate and five percent larger than the record of 11.8 million boxes set in 1979/80.</p>
<p>The California orange crop was forecast for 65.0 million boxes, up three percent from the previous forecast but two percent below last season's.</p>
</text>
